Z||000000||kornholio||09-30-2001||11:51 AM||||Hi,<BR>One of my headlight motors stays on when I lower the lights.  Does this mean that one relay is bad?  Or are the gears messed up?<P>I have done the "leave the headlights up" mod by wiring a switch to one of the wires a long time ago.  When I lower the lights, the one motor stays on.  When I hit the switch with the lights in the down position, it turns off the motor.<P>If it is a bad relay, where is it located and could I just get one from Radio Shack?<P>Thanks.<P>86 SE<p>[This message has been edited by kornholio (edited 09-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||BlackARROW||09-30-2001||12:00 PM||||Hehehe... I have the exact same setup as you.<P>I don't bother using that alternate switch, along with the others.<P>I don't really know what it is - a ground is not making somewhere obviously.<P>I will follow your post - give back a "Ok, I have fixed it this way" please  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>BlackARROW &gt;&gt;--&gt;<BR>Gadgeteered Fiero 2M4 '85<BR>"Get your groove on"||||reg||1
